From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: d3d11, dxgi: ID3D11Device5, ID3D11DeviceContext4, IDXGIDevice4; 16-bit float composition swap chains

Paint.NET asks for ID3D11DeviceContext3 and IDXGIDevice4 and fails without
them.
 - d3d11 devices are ID3D11Device3, 4 and 5: textures and queries of the
   new versions are created as the old; WriteToSubresource goes through
   UpdateSubresource; RegisterDeviceRemovedEvent never signals; fences are
   not supported.
 - Immediate contexts are ID3D11DeviceContext2, 3 and 4: tiled resources
   are not supported; annotation markers do nothing; Flush1 flushes and
   signals its event; hardware protection is off; Signal and Wait of fences
   are not supported.
 - DXGI devices are IDXGIDevice4: OfferResources1 succeeds and
   ReclaimResources1 reports the resources as kept.
 - Composition swap chains accept R16G16B16A16_FLOAT (Paint.NET's canvas).
   The frame is linear, and is sRGB encoded when drawn into the window.

Gate: test/wuicomp-gate.sh.
---
--- a/dlls/d3d11/device.c
+++ b/dlls/d3d11/device.c
@@ -473,7 +473,10 @@
 
     TRACE("iface %p, iid %s, out %p.\n", iface, debugstr_guid(iid), out);
 
-    if (IsEqualGUID(iid, &IID_ID3D11DeviceContext1)
+    if (IsEqualGUID(iid, &IID_ID3D11DeviceContext4)
+            || IsEqualGUID(iid, &IID_ID3D11DeviceContext3)
+            || IsEqualGUID(iid, &IID_ID3D11DeviceContext2)
+            || IsEqualGUID(iid, &IID_ID3D11DeviceContext1)
             || IsEqualGUID(iid, &IID_ID3D11DeviceContext)
             || IsEqualGUID(iid, &IID_ID3D11DeviceChild)
             || IsEqualGUID(iid, &IID_IUnknown))
